{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "021Y", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{smooth}$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\Sch/S)_{smooth}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Sch_{smooth}/S$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "MATH_0008": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{smooth}$", "MATH_0009": "$(\\Sch/S)_{smooth}$", "MATH_0010": "$U/S$", "MATH_0011": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{smooth}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0013": "$(\\Sch/S)_{smooth}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-section-localize}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-big-small-smooth}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fa9251d59f8864f6c61f9d0e4d0cabfed2971ea403b09ae114bddbcb6773bf82", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:44a13bd878726720834f5e0a4f8f04adc942bfeb47b340a0b617c9cfff04d111", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a big smooth\nsite containing <MATH_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The <TEXTITOPEN_0001>big smooth site of <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, denoted\n<MATH_0005>, is the site <MATH_0006>\nintroduced in Sites, Section <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0003> The <TEXTITOPEN_0002>big affine smooth site of <MATH_0007><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>, denoted\n<MATH_0008>, is the full subcategory of\n<MATH_0009> whose objects are affine <MATH_0010>.\nA covering of <MATH_0011> is any covering\n<MATH_0012> of <MATH_0013> which is a\nstandard smooth covering.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ebab98e9dc1c10883bf4847c6f1efe49373c3cebad17ce70dd89d88116886cf4", "unit_id": "tag:03X0:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "021Y", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:030abbc6ecdc114edec68dd307c0a7a43847d5de3d23c57d6a7a3507ea2b9b42", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNext, we check that the big affine site defines the same\ntopos as the big site.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:78c6b1773b894b6b6a83aad54cff4dcbe080120f2b8498c883a3a9768e16ad14", "unit_id": "tag:021Y:prose-0005"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "021Y", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{smooth}$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{smooth} \\to (\\Sch/S)_{smooth}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Sh((\\textit{Aff}/S)_{smooth})$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Sh((\\Sch/S)_{smooth})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-affine-big-site-smooth}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f19e45d484bc07e637d76004c7ef69fd90687e4213867932ee4080cc93bc0fa8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:12bdd0498ce73a4309b07d0f144dfc97f58dff1be40733b361eacbae94bdae87", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a big smooth\nsite containing <MATH_0003>.\nThe functor\n<MATH_0004>\nis special cocontinuous and induces an equivalence of topoi from\n<MATH_0005> to\n<MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:18c450a53ab57e6284fdba054e8db1977f35703113d69ae300bb0d75dcf3559f", "unit_id": "tag:06VC:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "021Y", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u : (\\textit{Aff}/S)_{smooth} \\to (\\Sch/S)_{smooth}$", "MATH_0002": "$T/S$", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "MATH_0004": "$T$", "MATH_0005": "$u$", "MATH_0006": "$u$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-special-cocontinuous-functor}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-lemma-equivalence}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-affine}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:62aba8c8ad188c45682859792b71a053c727afa965107a0ae860190886f8be9d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cb4dca2e7df02527b901d7b3f15f4049ba265ab134049b284050e3578b41633b", "source_text": "The notion of a special cocontinuous functor is introduced in\nSites, Definition <REF_0001>.\nThus we have to verify assumptions (1) -- (5) of\nSites, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nDenote the inclusion functor\n<MATH_0001>.\nBeing cocontinuous just means that any smooth covering of\n<MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003> affine, can be refined by a standard smooth covering of <MATH_0004>.\nThis is the content of\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nHence (1) holds. We see <MATH_0005> is continuous simply because a standard\nsmooth covering is a smooth covering. Hence (2) holds.\nParts (3) and (4) follow immediately from the fact that <MATH_0006> is\nfully faithful. And finally condition (5) follows from the\nfact that every scheme has an affine open covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f8e7787f82a992cb850d6e416ceae5d95e8b87039a585e321377d0496d55febb", "unit_id": "tag:06VC:proof"}
